    "lawCode": "Amd §131-g, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6535\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to providing that a county\nboard of supervisors shall be authorized to require that a ferry shall\ncarry without charge or fee of any kind for transportation any member of\nthe United States armed forces in uniform during their term of enlist-\nment in the service of the United States\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize a county board of supervisors to require ferries operating\nwithin such county to provide free transportation to any member of the\nUnited States armed forces in uniform during their term of enlistment in\nthe service of the State or the United States.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 131-g of the highway law to authorize a county\nboard of supervisors to require ferries operating within such county to\ncarry without charge or fee of any kind for transportation any member of\nthe United States armed forces in uniform during their term of enlist-\nment in the service of the United States, excluding municipal ferries\nthat are subject to the provisions of section 104 of the transportation\nlaw.\n\nSection 2. Is the severability clause.\n\nSection 3. Is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOur nation's service men and service women provide an invaluable service\nto our country and the State of New York, putting their lives at risk\nevery day for the greater good. This bill would allow a County, at their\ndiscretion, to require a waiver of charges or fees for ferry transporta-\ntion for these dedicated service members. This is just one of many ways\nto thank the brave men and women who have served our country.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
